    "standardized_narrative": "In 2019, Syndicate 1729 reported an overall deficit of GBP 1.8 million on prior year reserves, indicating a strengthening. This follows a GBP 9.0 million deficit in 2018. While the syndicate experienced favorable development on net losses from Hurricanes Irma and Michael and a profit from commuting a US Casualty contract, the overall prior year movement was adverse. The 2017 year of account was particularly affected by natural catastrophe losses from 2017 and 2018. Industry-wide trends of natural catastrophe loss creep and US Casualty reserve deterioration due to social inflation were noted, though the syndicate stated its own experience for these was not as severe.",
